      "diff": "@@ -34,15 +34,38 @@ wsbuglink:18734[].\n \n The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-// * wssalink:2023-09[]\n-// Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n-// wsbuglink:xxxxx[].\n+* wssalink:2023-09[]\n+RPCoRDMA dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:18852[].\n // cveidlink:2023-xxxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: b4c784805c\n-// Fixed in release-4.0: 4ec72ec3a1\n-// Fixed in release-3.6: 51e23ea7fd\n+// Fixed in master: 3c8be14c82\n+// Fixed in release-4.0: 04e506a337\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: c224405c31\n // CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n-// CWE-xxx\n+// CWE-126\n+// * Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2023-02-09-6781.pcap. wsbuglink:18852[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2023-10[]\n+LISP dissector large loop.\n+wsbuglink:18900[].\n+// cveidlink:2023-xxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: b911cf286f\n+// Fixed in release-4.0: 560f328cda\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 646b131303\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-834\n+// * Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2023-03-10-6859.pcap. wsbuglink:18900[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2023-11[]\n+GQUIC dissector crash\n+wsbuglink:18947[].\n+// cveidlink:2023-xxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: ee314ace8a\n+// Fixed in release-4.0: 9681566329\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 8970fc17e8\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-476\n+// * Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2023-03-31-6903.pcap. wsbuglink:18947[].\n \n The following bugs have been fixed:\n \n@@ -51,6 +74,19 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark keeps banging out random chords on your piano and yelling “LIPS LIKE SUGUAR, SUGAR KISSES” because it was funny that one time at a party.\n \n+* Wireshark ITS Dissector RTCMEM wrong protocol version selector 2 - should use 1 wsbuglink:18862[].\n+\n+* Wireshark treats the letter E in SSRC as an exponential representation of a number wsbuglink:18879[].\n+\n+* VNC RRE Parser skips over data wsbuglink:18883[].\n+\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2023-03-27-7564.pcap wsbuglink:18934[].\n+\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2023-03-31-6903.pcap wsbuglink:18947[].\n+\n+* RTP analysis shows incorrect timestamp error when timestamp is rolled over wsbuglink:18973[].\n+\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n // === Removed Features and Support\n@@ -67,15 +103,39 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.6.12.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+DNS\n+ERF\n+FF\n+genl\n+GQUIC\n+GSM A-bis OML\n+HL7\n+IEEE 802.11\n+ITS\n+ITS\n+LISP\n+netlink\n+netlink-netfilter\n+netlink-sock_diag\n+nl80211\n+RLC\n+RPCoRDMA\n+RTPS\n+SCTP\n+SMB\n+VNC\n+WCP\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// [commaize]\n-// --\n-// --\n+[commaize]\n+--\n+Netmon\n+NetScaler\n+--\n \n === New File Format Decoding Support\n \n",
